Description: Wake the multi-threaded session loop on exit
 Backport the session-owned semaphore and atomic exit flag from upstream
 PR #1201 so fuse_session_exit() wakes a loop blocked in sem_wait().
 .
 Keep the 3.14 worker-pool mutex and automatic session reset behavior.
 Check semaphore initialization and release it with the session. Publish
 the signal exit status before waking the loop, using release/acquire
 ordering so a signal delivered to another thread cannot lose its status.
 .
 Add mount-free custom-I/O regressions for direct, signal and worker exits,
 including repeated reuse of the same session.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/libfuse/libfuse/commit/7c22a19593c2b00fe6d2d44ac4c5e841629b26f3
Bug: https://github.com/libfuse/libfuse/issues/997
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: Bernd Schubert <bschubert@ddn.com>
Author: zhaoyingzhen <zhaoyingzhen@uniontech.com>
Last-Update: 2026-10-09

